{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": "./src",
    // 🔴 OFF, and it is not a performance oversight.
    //
    // nest-cli.json sets `deleteOutDir: true`, so every build wipes dist/
    // first. With `incremental` on, tsc then reads
    // tsconfig.build.tsbuildinfo, concludes every file is already emitted,
    // and writes NOTHING — while exiting 0.
    //
    // The result is an empty dist, a silent success, and `nest start`
    // dying on MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
    //
    // 🔴 WHERE THAT WAS MEASURED, because the first version of this
    // comment stated it as a fact about the project and it is a fact
    // about one toolchain. Observed on 04.10.2026 with @nestjs/cli
    // 10.4.9 and typescript 5.7.2 — the versions a drifted working copy
    // had installed. On the versions package-lock.json pins, 12.0.5 and
    // 6.0.3, which is what `npm ci` and therefore CI install, review
    // could NOT reproduce it: both passes emitted all 33 files. The
    // variable is the Nest CLI, not tsc.
    //
    // Kept off anyway, and the reason is cost, not fear: review measured
    // both builds at about 1.8 s either way across 107 non-spec files in
    // apps/api/src, so the flag buys nothing here, while leaving it on
    // reinstates a failure that looks exactly like success the moment
    // anyone's CLI slips back. scripts/ci/check-api-build-emits.sh does
    // not depend on the bug reproducing: its `--self-test` rehearses the
    // ASSERTION, so it stays meaningful whatever Nest does next.
    "incremental": false
  },
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "test", "dist", "**/*spec.ts"]
}
